// ============================================================================
// Interactions in the picked fields (Chapter 2): one knot per interactable in
// src/data/areas/borderland/pickedFields.ts. Draft text for the designer to rewrite.
// ============================================================================

=== picked_fields_hole ===
Somebody's hole. Dug out, sifted, given up on.
-> END

=== picked_fields_mast ===
A mast, or a pole, or an arm. Bent double, like something folded it.
Too heavy to carry, and too strange to sell.
-> END

=== picked_fields_hull ===
The back of something enormous, curved like a shell, sunk in the dirt.
Every panel that would come off has been prised off. The rest won't shift.
Nobody has ever dug down far enough to find where it ends.
-> END

=== picked_fields_glow ===
Down in a crack under the hull, something is still lit. A faint, steady light.
Nobody can get an arm in that far. People have tried.
-> END

=== picked_fields_glass ===
A slab of dark glass, cracked right across. You can see yourself in it, just.
-> END

=== picked_fields_tree ===
The tree. It's always there, at the edge of everything.
Its top goes up into the white and doesn't come down.
Nobody goes near it.
-> END

// --- People (draft) ---

=== picked_fields_friend ===
"Nothing out here but bolts and dirt. Same as yesterday." #speaker:scav_friend
"Still. Better than the queue." #speaker:scav_friend
-> END
